Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.150 --> 00:00:14.960 align:start position:0%
 
[Music]  [Music]  if you've seen elder ring all the way  through to the end then first of all  congratulations on your achievements  that is no small feat for a game as  challenging and massive as this one you  may also have some questions as to what  it all means did i get the good ending  or the bad ending after scouring through  countless item and enemy descriptions  lines of dialogue and so on i think i  have a pretty comprehensive picture of  some of the mythos behind the world of  elden ring and what its different  outcomes signify today i want to talk  about the age of the stars ending  specifically which is probably the most  talked about because well first of all  we are finally maidenless no more and  because out of all six endings this one  is probably the most ambiguous ronnie's  words as she brings forth her new age  are as cryptic as they are uncertain  there's talk of fear doubt and  loneliness and a dark path so what does  she have in store for the lands between  keep in mind that this is just my  interpretation it's very much possible  that i've missed or misinterpreted  certain things the amount of lore in  this game is massive and a lot of it  fractured and cryptic in nature if you  feel like i've missed something or you  want to give your own two cents on the  matter feel free to let me know down in  the comment section so we can all grow  wiser very well let us both learn  together  the night sky seems to play an important  role in alden ring everywhere you look  you can see remnants of stargazing  people mining for space debris a large  moon looming over the landscape and a  fearsome demigod who quite literally  held the stars in place with his power  over gravity what a badass as is common  in high fantasy the universe of eldon  ring does not function like our own and  we can find many clues from the story  writers which gives some more insight  among the starting classes in elden ring  is the astrologer who are said to be one  of the first to study the stars and are  also the precursors to the present day  sorcerers from the academy of raya  lucaria the ancient astrologers  discovered that beyond the stars of the  night sky lies a vast dark sea of  nothingness which they called the  primeval current it's also described as  a lightless void or an abyss on some  occasions it is believed that within  this void all life exists as one a sort  of singularity that holds all of life's  infinite possibilities from the void  stars and other celestial bodies are  born and these bodies hold fragments of  these possibilities also described as  residual life the astrologist theorized  that the very stars themselves are  essentially living beings life in a  primordial form yet holding a profound  wisdom and feigned cognition this  cognition is also referred to as the  wisdom of stone some of these celestial  bodies or pieces of it will eventually  rain down on the surface and when they  collide the residual life inside  fractures and evolves giving rise to  diverse and more complex life forms this  process is exemplified by some of the  creatures you may have encountered in  the lands between there's astol which is  said to be a malformed star born in the  lightless void far away the falling star  beasts found inside craters the  alabasters which are described as a race  of ancients who said to have risen to  life when a meteor struck long ago and  then there's the crystallines these  creatures are inorganic yet are alive  somehow and according to the shattering  crystal spell they are revered guests of  the sorcerers because they are the  living proof of the wisdom of stone and  the ideals of the primeval current the  sorcerers and alden ring are essentially  the scientists of this world they study  the cosmos at the raya lucaria academy  or hogwarts as i like to call it and  their magic practice which is referred  to as sorcery is derived from glindstone  pieces of crystallized space debris that  have rained down on the lands between  since time immemorial and are said to  house the very same residual life i  spoke about before these stones are  mined from caves or craters and use the  fashion and perfect spells and the  better your understanding of the cosmos  the more powerful your spells become  this is why sorcery spells and weapons  are commonly tied to the intelligence  attribute some saw the primeval current  as the holy grail of knowledge and  sorcery those obsessed with the abyss  even went as far as to replace parts of  their body or in some cases most of it  with glimstone crystals they believed  that through regression they could  harness the wisdom of stone and unravel  the mysteries of the abyss and draw  their magic from it also known as  primevo current sorcery which became a  controversial and forbidden practice in  the eyes of the academy the current was  apparently seen as something not to be  tampered with at least three people  including two headmasters have actually  been banished from the academy for  practicing this forbidden rite now there  is no text in the game that outright  confirms that the primeval current is  the origin of all life in the universe  but there is one piece of dialogue that  at least hints at this being the case  it's from an npc who's tied to the  questline that leads to the frenzied  flame ending and well just listen to  what she has to say all that there is  came from the one great  then came fractures  and births  and souls but the greater will made a  mistake  torment  despair  affliction every sin  every curse  every one born of the mistake  and so  what was borrowed  must be returned  melt it all away with the yellow chaos  flame  until all  is won again  so to break it down she says that all  there is came from the one great and  what was borrowed must one day return  until all is won again that sounds an  awful lot like the primeval current so  i'm guessing that she's probably talking  about the same thing followers of the  frenzied flames seem to believe that  life as it exists now is a mistake full  of pain suffering and division and would  rather see everything and everyone  disappear into the void from whence it  came which is exactly what happens when  you choose the frenzied flame ending if  my interpretations are correct it means  that those who study the cosmos  essentially discovered the true origin  of life itself problem is this discovery  and ideology is in direct opposition to  the greater will and the system it has  created the greater will is a being  classified as an outer god and is  responsible for the creation of the  elden ring as well as the earth tree  what outer gods are exactly is not  entirely clear it's some sort of  invisible divine presence likely far  beyond human comprehension call it  cosmic or interdimensional it's clear  that it's a being that operates from  outside reality as we know it hence the  outer part it's very lovecraftian which  is definitely nothing new for a  soulsborne title and yes there's more  than one outer god present in the lands  between at least six or seven are  theorized to exist each with their own  goals and motivations however only two  or possibly three have an actual impact  on the ending of the story and the  frenzied flame is one of them the  greater will happens to be the one with  the most power and influence in the  lands between at the time the story  takes place but it wasn't always like  that it is said that long ago it sent a  golden star into the lands between  carrying one of its representatives the  elden beast which is also the final boss  and after its arrival it started  establishing its own order many of its  followers are highly religious their  system of belief also known as the  golden order is based on the idea that  the greater will is the one true god and  anything that contradicts that belief is  deemed heresy  that  is a work of heresy its incantations  bear no lineage from the earth tree  it's a system that although based on the  concept of order is also extremely  intolerant ever since its inception it's  been at war with everyone around it even  enacting near genocide in some cases  those who stood against the house of the  artery or posed a threat in any way were  either wiped out forced into exile or  converted their beliefs and with every  victory the influence of the greater  will grew until it had little to no  adversaries left the only reason why the  academy escaped a similar fate was  because of an unexpected marriage the  marriage between the acting governor of  the academy queen ranala and a prominent  champion of the urtry ratagan of the  golden order who allegedly fell in love  on the battlefield because of this an  unusual alliance was formed between the  two ronnie was born from the marriage  between ranala and radigan and grew up  among the sorcerers during this alliance  over time she grew to despise the  greater will and all it stands for her  heart lay with the moon and the stars  and did not want to be controlled by a  god that rules with an iron fist even  since before the shattering of the alden  ring she had secretly been scheming to  bring about a new order one that would  replace the greater will entirely it's  also revealed that ronnie had a secret  mentor we don't know much about her but  she is described as a snow witch now  when the term witch is used in elden  ring it's usually not meant to be  positive this isn't like the harry  potter universe where males are wizards  and females are witches for example one  of the people i mentioned who were  kicked from the academy was selen an npc  who seems friendly at first until you  realize what she's done turns out that  she is also extremely obsessed with  primeval current sorcery even going as  far as to kill fellow students and  experimenting on them fusing their  bodies into one giant mass after being  banished from the academy and going into  hiding she was given the nickname the  grave and witch i don't necessarily  think that the snow witch had the same  malicious intent but the fact that she's  labeled as a witch does suggest that she  was at least practicing magic that was  deemed controversial or dangerous in the  world of sorcery it's also stated that  she taught ronnie to quote fear the dark  moon hence it's highly likely that her  secret mentor is the one who set ronnie  on her path to bring about the age of  the stars ronnie's questline essentially  sees you helping her in tying up the  final loose ends to make her new age  become a reality this is also why she  was so invested in the underground  cities of noxtella and nokron those who  built these cities were driven  underground and exiled when they  rebelled against the greater will not  only did they develop a weapon capable  of hurting the greater will but just  like the sorcerers they had a deep  connection with the cosmos  long ago the knocks invoked the ire of  the greater will and were banished deep  on the ground now they live under a  false sky in eternal anticipation of  their liege of the coming age of the  stars and their lord of night when you  stand before the elden ring and have  completed ronnie's questline instead of  restoring the alden ring and ensuring  the survival of the greater will you can  instead summon ronnie's spirit after  which she dissolves the alden ring and  ushers in her new age but what exactly  is the age of the stars and what does it  mean for the future of the lands between  well let's listen to what she has to say  i thought i might expound a little  further upon the order i envision  mine will be an order not of gold  but the stars and moon of the chill  night  i would keep them far from the earth  beneath our feet  as it is now life and souls and order  abound tightly together  but i would have them at a great remove  and have the certainties of sight  emotion faith and touch all become  impossibilities  which is why i would abandon this soil  with mine order  words thou come to me even now  my one and only lord  the way i interpret it is that ronnie is  creating a universe closer to that of  her own she says that she will keep the  stars and moon far away from the earth  implying that before the age of the  stars they exist at a much closer  proximity i don't know if that's true i  mean they seem pretty far away then  again the fact that they constantly  invade the lands between also speaks  volumes like she says under the greater  will life souls and order are bound  together which is true it's it's right  there right there believing in god is  not exactly hard when it and its rules  are literally staring you right in the  face in her age there will be life there  will still be order but that order will  be so far removed from mankind that  absolute faith and knowledge of its  existence will become an impossibility  creating doubts fear and loneliness and  i don't want to get too philosophical  but it is kind of like our reality as  far as we know at least right now we are  alone in the cosmos with a lot of doubts  fears of what happens when we die and  questions of where we came from and why  we even exist some suggest that the dark  moon she mentions is yet another outer  god but i honestly have my doubts about  that i couldn't find any text that  specifically says that the dark moon is  an outer god not to mention it kinda  goes against what ronnie stands for i  mean she purposely rid herself of her  empyrean body for the exact reason of  not wanting to be bound to an outer god  anymore to free herself from those  shackles and walk her own path a path  that leads into the dark abyss of the  cosmos and the lord of night mentioned  before likely refers to you the  protagonist because in every ending you  become the lord of something elden lord  lord of chaos and in this case you  become ronnie's lord as you set off into  the cosmos together my current take is  that the dark moon is supposed to be  symbolic a harbinger if you will if you  look at the landscape of the lands  between there's two prominent entities  that stick out the ur tree and right  next to it a moon a moon on the verge of  turning dark perhaps meant as a sign  that the age of the earth tree is coming  to a close and the age of the stars is  about to commence if you choose that  ending of course whether or not you  found this to be a good ending really  depends on your point of view do you  think it's better to have god right  there in front of you dictating your  every move or would you rather embrace  ignorance and the mysteries of the  universe or maybe you just want to press  that history eraser button be sure to  let me know which ending you find the  most satisfying i skipped over a lot of  details when it comes to ronnie herself  and her backstory because well that  could easily take up an entire video on  its own luckily there just so happens to  be a certain bandit i know who made an  amazing video on that exact topic so if  you will please go and check it out  ronnie has one of the most interesting  and equally mysterious character stories  in the entire game so it'll no doubt be  worth your time thank you all so much  for watching and i hope you found my  first eldering theory to be entertaining  a big thanks to wes and sabrina for  joining my patreon and to wavery and  ashley hall for becoming a channel  member you guys are amazing i must  apologize for the time it took me to  make this video elden ringlore is a lot  more complicated and convoluted than  zeldalore it was honestly a bit  overwhelming i may have also been  hopelessly addicted to playing the game  the past weeks which wasn't exactly  great for productivity either but hey at  least i had a good time with it and that  is all for now this is dawn signing off  and  have a good one  [Music]  [Music]  [Music]  you

